  "title": "Three Sinkings, One Stewardess: Five Years, No Deaths",
  "description": "Meet Violet Jessop, an Irish stewardess who defied the odds. In just five years, she was aboard three of the world's most famous ships during catastrophic events.\n\nFrom a collision with a warship to two famous sinkings, her story is one of sheer luck and survival.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"Violet Jessop\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violet_Jessop), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImages from Wikimedia Commons:\nViolet Jessop in Voluntary Aid Detachment Uniform.jpg (Anonymous Unknown author, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Violet_Jessop_in_Voluntary_Aid_Detachment_Uniform.jpg\nThe SS Belgenland.jpg (Harland &amp; Wolff, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_SS_Belgenland.jpg\nViolet Jessop in Voluntary Aid Detachment Uniform.jpg (Anonymous Unknown author, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Violet_Jessop_in_Voluntary_Aid_Detachment_Uniform.jpg\nViolet Jessop in Voluntary Aid Detachment Uniform (cropped).jpg (Originally loaded to en-wiki by Boylo, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Violet_Jessop_in_Voluntary_Aid_Detachment_Uniform_(cropped).jpg\n\n3D models:\nTitanic by 6F5Jedi (CC BY 4.0) https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/none-465f425b342a41118f78c83758eaab39",
